  "submitted_text": "Step 1: Determine the side length of one of the equilateral triangles.\nSince the perimeter of one of the equilateral triangles is 21 inches, and an equilateral triangle has three equal sides, we divide the perimeter by 3 to find the side length.\nSide length = 21 inches / 3 = 7 inches\n\nStep 2: Recognize the relationship between the hexagon and the triangles.\nA regular hexagon can be divided into six equilateral triangles, and each side of the hexagon is equal to the side length of these triangles.\n\nStep 3: Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon.\nThe perimeter of the hexagon is the sum of its six sides. Since each side is 7 inches, the perimeter is:\nPerimeter = 6 * 7 inches = 42 inches\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{42}",
